---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DIG, SUPPORT, SERVICE } from "../config/brand";
---

<Base
  title="Support — WOIII.me"
  description="Help with the WOIII.me Chrome extension, the ChatGPT and Claude plugins, Discogs sign-in, results, privacy requests and security reports."
  bodyClass="privacy-page"
  headerVariant="overlay"
>
  <section class="section privacy-section" data-header-tone="dark">
    <div class="wrap policy">
      <h1>{SERVICE.name} <span class="accent">support</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Help with the Chrome extension, the ChatGPT and Claude plugins, Discogs
        sign-in, unexpected results, privacy requests and security reports.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 21 October 2026 · {SERVICE.name} was previously called {SERVICE.formerName}.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT.email}`}>{SUPPORT.email}</a>. Say whether
        you use the Chrome extension, ChatGPT or Claude, what you asked or which
        Discogs page you had open, and what happened. You can also use{" "}
        <a href={DIG.issuesUrl}>GitHub Issues</a>{" "}for reproducible bugs or{" "}
        <a href={DIG.discussionsUrl}>Discussions</a>{" "}for questions and ideas.
      </p>

      <h2>Do not send secrets</h2>
      <p>
        Never send a password, Discogs personal access token, OAuth token,
        client secret, API key, MFA or one-time code, private collection export,
        or another person's personal data. Crop or redact screenshots when the
        detail is not needed to diagnose the problem.
      </p>

      <h2>Chrome extension</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open a release or master page on discogs.com, then click the {SERVICE.name} icon to open the side panel.</li>
        <li>Choose <em>Connect with Discogs</em> and approve access on the Discogs page that opens. If nothing opens, allow pop-ups for the extension and try again.</li>
        <li>"Discogs needs a minute" means the Discogs rate limit, which all users share, is used up for the moment. Wait the time shown and choose <em>Try again</em>.</li>
        <li>If the panel shows <em>Finish update</em>, click it to reload the extension.</li>
        <li>Still stuck: sign out on the settings page (the gear), then connect again. Signing out clears the extension's data from your device.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>ChatGPT and Claude</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Add {SERVICE.name} from the app directory in ChatGPT or Claude where it is listed, or add a custom connector with the server address <code>https://{SERVICE.serverHost}/mcp</code>.</li>
        <li>Complete the Discogs sign-in in the same browser session when your assistant asks you to connect.</li>
        <li>Ask in plain words, for example "What's the best-sounding pressing of Kind of Blue?" or paste a Discogs release link.</li>
        <li>If your assistant says the connection expired or was revoked, disconnect {SERVICE.name} in your assistant's settings and connect again.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Results and limitations</h2>
      <p>
        {SERVICE.name} is read-only. It cannot buy records, contact sellers,
        change your collection or wantlist, or submit ratings, and it shows no
        prices. Scores are estimates built from Discogs catalogue and community
        data and published pressing knowledge; they are not measurements of
        sound quality. Discogs data can be incomplete, user-contributed or
        changed after a result was shown. If a score looks wrong, send us the
        Discogs link and what you expected.
      </p>

      <h2>Delete your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Revoke {SERVICE.name} in your Discogs settings, under <em>Applications</em>.</li>
        <li>Sign out of the extension or uninstall it.</li>
        <li>Disconnect the plugin or connector in ChatGPT or Claude.</li>
        <li>Ask your assistant to reset your {SERVICE.name} settings.</li>
        <li>
          To have your sign-in grant and settings deleted from our server, email{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT.email}`}>{SUPPORT.email}</a> with "Privacy
          request" in the subject and your Discogs username.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        For access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection or a copy of
        your data, email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT.email}`}>{SUPPORT.email}</a>{" "}
        with "Privacy request" in the subject. We answer within one month. The{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> lists what we process, where, and
        for how long.
      </p>

      <h2>Security reports</h2>
      <p>
        Report a suspected credential exposure, authorisation bypass or data
        disclosure privately by email before opening a public issue. Do not
        exploit it beyond what is needed to show it, do not access another
        user's account, and do not include live credentials in the report.
      </p>

      <h2>Response expectations</h2>
      <p>
        {SERVICE.name} is an independent project, not a staffed service desk.
        We aim to reply within a few working days. For an urgent account
        concern, revoke {SERVICE.name} under Discogs <em>Applications</em>{" "}
        straight away; that stops all access to your account.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-section {
    --accent-hue: #c8ff9f;
    background: #000;
    padding-block: 170px 104px;
  }
  .privacy-section > .policy {
    --text-width: 62rem;
    width: min(100%, 1440px);
    max-width: 1440px;
    padding-inline: clamp(24px, 3.35vw, 48px);
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 7);
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 2.5);
    padding-top: calc(var(--space) * 4);
    max-width: var(--text-width);
  }
  .policy ol,
  .policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25em;
    display: grid;
    gap: calc(var(--space) * 1.5);
    max-width: var(--text-width);
  }
  .policy li::marker {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .policy p {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 2);
  }
  .updated {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-tertiary);
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 3);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .privacy-section {
      padding-block: 125px 64px;
    }
  }
</style>
